Slanted single wall inserts (RHD, RRHD), high energy efficiency with less losses over the entire pressure level and high pressure tolerance over an extended fluid range. To improve efficiency, the inserts can be inserted between two tubes which are parallel to the axis at an angle of 50deg.
RHD - Rail type single wall inserts for standard tube connections for the oil market with more than 3 bar pressure tolerance;
RRHD - Railtype single wall inserts with more than max. max. design pressure for installations with pressure from 10 bar to 16 bar;
RHD - Slanting version;
RRHD with angled connection to the header pipe without header joint or hub, pressure up to 4 bar;
RHS - Slantinversion version for flanged ends on the head pipes, higher pressure than RHD;
RHR - Slantenversion version for welded ends on the header pipes, higher pressures than RHS;
W - Slant conversion for connection connections flanged to flanged, higher pressure
